## Create React Native project {% #create-react-project %}

Create a React Native app with the `create-expo-app` command.
This tutorial uses React Navigation for routing, so start from the blank template. The default template uses Expo Router instead.

```sh
npx create-expo-app@latest ideas-tracker --template blank
cd ideas-tracker
```

## Add dependencies {% #add-dependencies %}

Install the React Native Appwrite SDK.

```sh
npx expo install react-native-appwrite react-native-url-polyfill
```

Then, install React Navigation to help implement simple navigation logic.

```sh
npm install @react-navigation/native @react-navigation/native-stack
```

Install peer dependencies needed for React Navigation.

```sh
npx expo install react-native-screens react-native-safe-area-context
```
